WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:03.060
- [Narrator] The economic
ruptures caused by Russia's war

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.130
in Ukraine triggered a
string of street protests

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.500
in Moldova over the past
few months, and recently led

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.590
to the collapse of the country's
pro-European government.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:13.200
Another pro-western prime
minister, Dorin Recean,

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.160
took over on Thursday

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.810
amid heightened security threats linked

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:17.220
to the war next door.

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.050
That's because the former Soviet Republic

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:20.880
is strategically important to both Russia

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.250
and Ukraine as the war rages on.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:24.083
Here's why.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.990
Moldova is a small,
landlocked country sandwiched

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:31.530
between Romania and the West
and Ukraine to the east.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.320
It has a population smaller
than that of Chicago

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:37.830
and the third lowest GDP per
capita of any European country.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.180
Its already struggling economy

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:42.030
has taken a hit since
war broke out in Ukraine.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.890
Inflation has soared
amid Moscow's decision

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.390
to squeeze natural gas supplies,

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:47.313
prompting a wave of street protests,

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.040
and Russian attacks on the electrical grid

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.640
in Ukraine have led to power
cuts for its tiny neighbor,

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.587
while an influx of Ukrainian refugees

00:00:55.587 --> 00:00:57.993
has strained Moldova's public services.

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.600
The situation comes at a time

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.040
when the country is cooperating closely

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.010
with NATO and seeking to
join the European Union.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:09.180
- It is on a real
pro-reform, anti-corruption

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:11.010
and European path.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.510
- [Narrator] This has
worsened Moldova's relations

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:13.828
with Russia.

00:01:13.828 --> 00:01:15.870
Some pro-Western politicians
in Moldova and Ukraine

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:16.703
have accused the Kremlin

00:01:16.703 --> 00:01:19.566
of planning a coup to
destabilize the country.

00:01:19.566 --> 00:01:24.316
(Volodymyr speaking in foreign language)

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.300
- [Narrator] On February 9th,

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.280
Ukraine's president said
he had shared intelligence

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.690
with his Moldovan counterpart

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.950
about an alleged Russian scheme

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:34.980
to topple her country's
democratic system of government.

00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:37.800
A day later, Moldova's
pro-Western government collapsed

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.710
citing the economic challenges
brought on by the war.

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:41.910
And not long after that,

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.920
the country's president said
she had confirmed details

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.090
of Zelenskyy's statement

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:46.680
and that Russia's plan included attacks

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.023
on government buildings
and taking hostages.

00:01:50.056 --> 00:01:54.389
(Maia speaking in foreign language)

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.440
- [Narrator] Russia dismissed
the allegations as unfounded,

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:03.390
saying Ukraine was
attempting to draw Moldova

00:02:03.390 --> 00:02:05.730
into a confrontation with Moscow.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:06.900
The US said it hadn't been able

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.273
to independently confirm
the alleged coup plot.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:15.000
- What I'll say about that
is deeply concerning reports,

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.890
certainly not outside the
bounds of Russian behavior

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:21.810
- [Narrator] A destabilized
Moldova is in Russia's interest

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:23.010
according to one analyst

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:26.040
and could pose a security
threat to Western Ukraine.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.510
Russia has troops stationed

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:29.370
in the breakaway region of Transnistria.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.320
The thin strip of land on
Moldova's eastern border

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:34.470
with Ukraine is run by
pro-Russian separatists.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:37.110
If Ukraine had to allocate
resources to counter that threat,

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:39.600
it could diminish the chances
of success in the southeast

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.250
of the country the analysts said.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:43.320
These factors raised fears

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:45.600
that the war could spill
out beyond Ukraine's borders

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.610
and highlight the important
role Moldova might play

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:49.684
for both sides in the coming months.

00:02:49.684 --> 00:02:52.351
(pensive music)

